It is early evening.
The rain finally stops.
The clouds disappear.
The city smells fresh and cool.
I fetch my backpack from the cloakroom.
Then I walk out of the museum.
Normally I take the U-Bahn for this route.
But this evening is so beautiful.
I walk the whole way to my flat on foot.
The streets are very quiet.
Five months ago, everything here was new and unfamiliar.
Now I belong here.
The rest of the summer still lies ahead of me.
I am really looking forward to this time.
Next week it is my birthday.
I am turning thirty-two years old.
Life in Berlin is really beautiful.
